\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Convention}
\title{Fixed-budget trace-selection protocol}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{harness}

\p{The trace intervention is a finite evaluation proposal. It compares
horizon and selector effects at a fixed retained budget while keeping the
model, teacher, scaffold, task split, verifier, seed law, and total token and
compute budgets visible. The source's selective-refinement intervention
supplies the comparison pattern, but the following arm matrix is an FTIP
protocol rather than a source result
\citet{Sections 6-7; Tables 4-5, 10}{dang2026selecting}.}

\p{Let #{\mathcal A} be the finite P0 arm-label set, with its declared
boundary map #{r:\mathcal A\to\mathcal J}. Refine it with finite horizon labels
#{\mathfrak H_{\rm hor}\subset\mathbb N}, selector labels
#{\mathfrak L_{\rm sel}}, reset masks #{\mathfrak M_{\rm reset}:=\mathcal
P(\{s,h,w\})} from \ref{ftip-00P0}, budget labels
#{\mathfrak B_{\rm budget}}, split labels #{\mathfrak D_{\rm split}}, and a
finite randomization-label set #{\mathfrak R_{\rm lbl}}. Let
#{M:\mathcal A\to\mathfrak M_{\rm reset}} be the declared P0 reset-mask map.
A law map
#{\lambda_{\rm R}:\mathfrak R_{\rm lbl}\to\operatorname{Law}(\mathcal G)}
assigns each label its declared paired randomization law. Each experimental arm
is a tuple}
##{
 a=(a_0,H,\ell,B,D,\eta)\in
 \mathcal A\times\mathfrak H_{\rm hor}\times\mathfrak L_{\rm sel}
 \times\mathfrak B_{\rm budget}
 \times\mathfrak D_{\rm split}\times\mathfrak R_{\rm lbl},
}
\p{where #{a_0} is the P0 arm label, #{r(a_0)} is its declared boundary,
#{M(a_0)} is its P0 reset mask, and
#{\mathcal R_a:=\lambda_{\rm R}(\eta)} is its paired law.
Each arm declares one model, teacher,
scaffold, verifier, task law, and inference protocol; those are held fixed
across its paired reset and continue runs. The arm's split #{D} declares
pairwise-disjoint selection and held-out task sets #{Q_{\rm sel}(D)} and
#{Q_{\rm hold}(D)} with #{|Q_{\rm hold}(D)|>0}, plus any cross-benchmark
split. The mask #{M(a_0)} is the P0 reset mask, so the transition is
#{\mathsf{Reset}_{r(a_0),M(a_0)}}.}

\p{Cross horizon and selection with the state masks in
\ref{ftip-00P0}. Each mask clears a selected subset of session context,
candidate history, and workspace coordinates; the lifecycle transition retains
the verified best candidate and its artifact. At minimum compare:}
\ol{
  \li{one-stage full-long traces;}
  \li{verification-preserving intermediate truncation;}
  \li{warm-start plus top-likelihood selection;}
  \li{warm-start plus bottom-likelihood selection;}
  \li{warm-start plus random selection at the same retained budget; and}
  \li{a coverage-stratified or diversity-preserving selector.}
}

\p{For arm #{a} and a positive run count #{N_a\in\mathbb N_{>0}}, with run
index #{i\in\{1,\ldots,N_a\}}, use the event-time domain
#{\overline{\mathbb N}:=\mathbb N\cup\{+\infty\}} and the convention
#{\inf\varnothing:=+\infty}. The run receipt supplies measurable event
indicators #{E^{\rm term}_{a,i,t}}, #{E^{\rm ev}_{a,i,t}},
#{E^{\rm ver}_{a,i,t}},
#{E^{\rm fail}_{a,i,t}}, and #{E^{\rm rec}_{a,i,t}} from a declared finite
event alphabet, a measurable task-value score #{u_{a,i}(t)}, and a finite
saturation threshold #{u^{\rm sat}_a}. Define}
##{
 \tau_{a,i}:=\inf\{t:E^{\rm term}_{a,i,t}=1\},\quad
 \tau^{\rm ev}_{a,i}:=\inf\{t:E^{\rm ev}_{a,i,t}=1\},\quad
 \tau^{\rm ver}_{a,i}:=\inf\{t:E^{\rm ver}_{a,i,t}=1\},
}
##{
 \tau^{\rm fail}_{a,i}:=\inf\{t:E^{\rm fail}_{a,i,t}=1\},\quad
 \tau^{\rm rec}_{a,i}:=\inf\{t:E^{\rm rec}_{a,i,t}=1\},\quad
 \tau^{\rm sat}_{a,i}:=\inf\{t:u_{a,i}(t)\ge u^{\rm sat}_a\}.
}
\p{Define the measurable predicates #{G_{a,i}} for bounded evidence,
verification, and recovery by}
##{
 G_{a,i}:=\mathbf 1[\tau^{\rm ev}_{a,i}<\tau_{a,i},\
 \tau^{\rm ver}_{a,i}<\tau_{a,i},\
 (\tau^{\rm fail}_{a,i}\ge\tau_{a,i}\ \mathord\lor\
 \tau^{\rm fail}_{a,i}<\tau^{\rm rec}_{a,i}<\tau_{a,i})],
}
\p{#{F_{a,i}:=\mathbf 1[\tau^{\rm fail}_{a,i}<\tau_{a,i}]} records a
failure before termination, and #{V_{a,i}:=\mathbf 1[\tau^{\rm ver}_{a,i}<\infty]}
records a verifier pass. A recovery follows a failure exactly when
#{\tau^{\rm fail}_{a,i}<\tau^{\rm rec}_{a,i}<\tau_{a,i}}. Define the measurable indicators}
##{
 I^{\rm pre}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[\tau_{a,i}<\tau^{\rm ev}_{a,i}],\qquad
 I^{\rm prod}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[G_{a,i}],\qquad
 I^{\rm over}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[\tau_{a,i}>\tau^{\rm sat}_{a,i}],
}
##{
 I^{\rm rec}_{a,i}=\mathbf 1[\tau^{\rm fail}_{a,i}<\tau^{\rm rec}_{a,i}<\tau_{a,i}],\qquad
 I^{\rm ver}_{a,i}=V_{a,i}.
}
\p{The corresponding run rates use the declared denominator #{N_a}:}
##{
 (\widehat p^{\rm pre}_a,\widehat p^{\rm prod}_a,\widehat p^{\rm over}_a,
 \widehat p^{\rm rec}_a,\widehat p^{\rm ver}_a)
 =\frac1{N_a}\sum_{i=1}^{N_a}
 (I^{\rm pre}_{a,i},I^{\rm prod}_{a,i},I^{\rm over}_{a,i},I^{\rm rec}_{a,i},I^{\rm ver}_{a,i}).
}
\p{Let #{A_{a,i}} be the indicator that the receipt is complete, no protocol
violation occurred, and its run task #{q_{a,i}} lies in #{Q_{\rm hold}(D)}.
For the finite held-out task set, task coverage is}
##{
 \widehat C^{\rm task}_a:=
 \frac{|\{q\in Q_{\rm hold}(D):\exists i,\ q_{a,i}=q,\ A_{a,i}=1\}|}
 {|Q_{\rm hold}(D)|}.
}
\p{For a declared finite strategy-label set
#{\mathfrak S_{\rm strat,a}} with #{|\mathfrak S_{\rm strat,a}|>0}, strategy
coverage is}
##{
 \widehat C^{\rm strat}_a:=
 \frac{|\{s\in\mathfrak S_{\rm strat,a}:
 s\text{ appears in an admitted held-out trace}\}|}
 {|\mathfrak S_{\rm strat,a}|}.
}
\p{These positive denominators are reported with the arm receipt.}

\p{Let #{X^{\rm sel}_{a,i}} collect the selection-time prefix, teacher-forced
selector score, data-only trace metadata, and the arm's training/selection
split, with the metadata map declared to exclude held-out outcomes, verifier
outcomes, and post-selection continuation events. Define
#{\mathcal F^{\rm sel}_{a,i}:=\sigma(X^{\rm sel}_{a,i})}. The selector is
measurable with respect to this sigma-field. Pair every selected trace with
its unselected continuation under the same arm law, and reserve
#{Q_{\rm hold}(D)} and the cross-benchmark split for evaluation only.}

\p{The protocol charges selection, storage, restart, discarded-trace, and
verification costs, and retains the task, selector, budget, split, seed, and
randomization receipts. No claim that selected traces improve FTIP behavior is
established until an immutable experiment record contains these fields and the
finite rates and coverage denominators above.}

\p{No formal declaration corresponding to this finite protocol is claimed
here; it remains an empirical evaluation proposal until an implementation
supplies the stated receipts and measurable interfaces.}
